returned_finding_id	P1-public-raw-v11-executor-bypasses-sealed-intake
returned_finding	The exported runV11({authority,evidenceRoot,runCommand}) accepts a caller-provided authority.target and immediately creates evidence then issues Docker inspection and psql commands. It never calls intakeV11, never validates candidate/registry/DB/QA/security/drain/resource SHA inputs, and can be imported directly. The static test itself proves that callable raw path by invoking runV11 with only {target}.
impact	No-pre-review execution is not fail-closed. The candidate authority's execution_authorized=true can be combined with the publicly reachable raw executor to bypass the declared DB→QA→security→drain→resource gate, regardless of the otherwise complete A-H/v4 registry.
required_correction	Do not export any target-accepting raw execution function. Make the sole executable entry invoke intakeV11 internally and pass its sealed result to a private executor, or move raw execution to an unimportable private implementation. Add an import-level regression showing absent/incomplete/mismatched review chain produces zero child/Docker calls even when candidate authority says execution_authorized=true.

returned_finding_id_2	P2-required-review-resource-artifacts-not-yet-present
returned_finding_2	At review time no v11 DB, QA, security, drain, or resource authority artifacts exist in the task research directory. The candidate is therefore appropriately static, but no future GO can be asserted until those five immutable artifacts are independently generated and checked for exact acyclic bindings.
impact_2	The stated acyclic chain is unexercised against real immutable review files.
required_correction_2	After P1 is corrected, create fresh readonly DB, QA, security, drain, and resource artifacts in order; independently verify the SHA bindings and resource freshness before any execution authorization is issued.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute-until-P1-corrected-and-fresh-review-chain-exists
